ning I see his picture  I'll talk to him about it saying they're  still working on it so I pray there will  be people who will watch this interview  and they'll think to themselves  hazing has been happening for decades  sure what hope is there really that it's  ever gonna end well if we don't do  something it definitely is not going to  end you're just not supposed to bury  your kids they've joined with the  coffee's and more than a dozen other  surviving families to form push parents  United to stop hazing which includes the  Piazza family whose son Tim died at Penn  State last winter together they're  rallying for justice how do you break  the cycle accountability and education a  federal statute has to be written that  goes from the top you know where the  national fraternity is at risk as well  as the local chapter and then education  to high school students and if they  succeed their hope is that push never  adds a new member it's about legacy yeah  yeah if we keep his spirit alive then  he's not dead  if this can go to Washington DC it could  be the Andrew coffee law is that  something you'd like to see yes can't be  for nothing I mean no can't can't have  died for nothing  has to be purpose and there is purpose  shortly after Andrews death Florida  State University acted swiftly in  temporarily banning Greek life but FSU  president tells us there is still room  for improvement I don't want it to  happen again on our campus and I hope  other campuses are paying attention to  what we're doing because I think I think  we are making progress but I will say  this I think Greek life as we know it  today has to change has to change in  order for us to move forward with the  positive things that the Greek community  does the coffees and all the victims  families say it's important for schools  to step up and have stricter policies  across the board on this may be a  one-and-done rule yes that president is  so right it has to change and just  because it's been happening for decades  doesn't make it right I love whoever  said hazing is a byproduct of peer  pressure yeah that was lawyerly feel the  coffee's pain because you know when you  take your kids to school you're going to  Bed Bath &amp; Beyond you're picking up  pillowcases and duvets they remember  reading the jaws a story back in  February never thinking would apply to  their life and then months later your  piece should be shown every college  student that's going away it really  should the parents would like that the  pictures of Andrew coffee so much  promise still yet ahead of him that's  what's makes them so much life I think  the message is that just like drunk  driving hazing is always risky and  always wrong that's what the parents  want people to take away from this
 

